{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2156-12-16 20:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I’ll be taking care of you during this admission. You came in with worsening abdominal pain and nausea. Can you tell me more about what’s been going on?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2156-12-16 20:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yeah, the pain started about four days ago. It’s in my upper belly, kind of wrapping around to the right side. It’s like my usual pain, but worse. I was in the hospital a few days ago but left AMA because I felt a little better. Now it’s back."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2156-12-16 20:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. And have you been able to keep anything down? Any vomiting?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2156-12-16 20:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yeah, I’ve been throwing up a lot. I can’t eat much. My GJ tube hasn’t been working right either."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2156-12-16 20:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay, we’ll check on that. We gave you some Zofran and Dilaudid in the ER for nausea and pain. How’s the pain now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2156-12-16 20:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "A little better, but still pretty bad. I need something stronger sometimes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2156-12-16 20:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll keep managing it with IV Dilaudid as needed. We also did a chest X-ray to check for other issues, but your lungs look clear. The Port-A-Cath and your GJ tube are visible, but we’ll need to confirm if the tube is in the right place."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2156-12-16 20:37:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I didn’t want the X-ray, but okay. Is my tube really the problem?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2156-12-16 20:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It might be. You mentioned it wasn’t working well. We’ll look into it. For now, we’re treating this as acute on chronic pancreatitis, which fits your symptoms."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2156-12-16 20:39:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s what I always get. But why does it keep happening?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2156-12-16 20:40:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Chronic pancreatitis means your pancreas is already damaged. Things like poor nutrition, diabetes, and even the tube issues can flare it up. We’ll focus on controlling pain, stopping vomiting, and making sure your tube works."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2156-12-17 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your labs from last night show your blood sugar was high at 342, but your white count is normal. No signs of infection. Your electrolytes were a bit off, but we’re correcting them."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2156-12-17 08:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "My sugars are always high. I take Lantus at night, but I haven’t been eating, so I wasn’t sure how much to take."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2156-12-17 08:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve lowered your Lantus to 20 units at bedtime because you’re not eating much. When you start eating again, you’ll need to increase it. We’ll talk more about that later."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2156-12-17 08:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, but I don’t like changing my insulin. I have a routine."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2156-12-17 08:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I understand. We’re doing this to keep your sugars safe. Too much insulin when you’re not eating can cause lows. We’ll help you adjust when you’re ready."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2156-12-17 08:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Fine. What about my tube? Can we fix it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2156-12-17 08:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re planning to replace it. The team from Interventional Radiology will do it tomorrow. You mentioned the last tube type didn’t work well for you?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2156-12-17 08:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, the MIC one. I need the other kind—the one I had before. It works better with my feeds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2156-12-17 08:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Noted. We’ll make sure they use the one you prefer. The procedure is quick—done over a wire so they don’t have to start from scratch."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2156-12-18 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your pain is looking better. You’ve had Dilaudid and Compazine, and you haven’t vomited since yesterday. How are you feeling?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2156-12-18 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Better, yeah. Still sore, but not as intense. Can I try eating something?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2156-12-18 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We can start with small sips. But we’re waiting until after your tube replacement tomorrow. We want to make sure the new tube is working before you rely on it or eat too much by mouth."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2156-12-18 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "But what if the new tube doesn’t work either?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2156-12-18 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The radiology report shows the old tube was in the right place, so the issue might be with how it’s used. The new one should work. We’ll test it after placement."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2156-12-19 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news—your tube was successfully replaced this morning. They used the type you wanted, and it’s now in place."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2156-12-19 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great! Can I start my feeds now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2156-12-19 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we started a slow feed today. But we’ll monitor for residuals—if too much stays in, we may need to hold it for a bit. Your gastroparesis can slow stomach emptying."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2156-12-19 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I hate when that happens. It feels like I’m full all the time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2156-12-19 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll go slow. We also switched your Protonix to Prevacid Solutab. It dissolves better and works in the tube. Protonix doesn’t dissolve well when crushed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2156-12-19 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, as long as I can take it through the tube."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2156-12-20 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We started concentrated tube feeds today. How are you tolerating them?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2156-12-20 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel okay. No vomiting. But I’m still not hungry."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2156-12-20 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s expected. The feeds will help with nutrition. Your blood sugar was 251 yesterday—still high, but better. Keep taking your insulin as we adjusted."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2156-12-20 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m trying. But I don’t want to go low."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2156-12-20 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll help you adjust as you eat more. For now, 20 units is safe. You’ll need to increase it later—talk to your PCP about that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2156-12-21 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve done well. Pain is controlled, no nausea, and you’re tolerating the tube feeds. We’re thinking about discharge tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2156-12-21 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Really? That’s good. But what about my pain meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2156-12-21 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll give you a one-week supply of Dilaudid—same dose you take at home. No refills, as per policy. You’ll need to see your PCP for more."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2156-12-21 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I can do that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2156-12-21 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We also want to check the tube placement before you leave, just to be sure it’s working."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2156-12-21 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I don’t want to do that. I feel fine. The tube is working."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2156-12-21 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I understand, but it’s important. If it’s not in the right place, your feeds could go into your stomach and cause issues."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2156-12-21 09:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I just don’t want another test. Can’t we just assume it’s okay?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2156-12-21 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We can’t assume. But if you refuse, we’ll document that. Just please check at home and call your doctor if there’s any problem."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2156-12-22 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. We’re ready to discharge you. You’re alert, walking, and your pain is controlled."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2156-12-22 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great. What do I need to do when I get home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2156-12-22 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Keep taking your new Prevacid instead of Protonix. Take your insulin—20 units at night for now, but increase as you eat more. Call your PCP for refills and to review all your meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2156-12-22 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the tube?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2156-12-22 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re unsure if it’s working because you declined the check. Please verify at home. If you have pain, swelling, or can’t run feeds, call your doctor right away."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2156-12-22 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll check it. I think it’s fine."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2156-12-22 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Also, follow up with your PCP soon. And if pain worsens or you can’t keep fluids down, come back."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2156-12-22 08:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thanks for helping me feel better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2156-12-22 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take care, and we’re here if you need us."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2156-12-16 20:16:00",
    "admission_end": "2156-12-22 10:31:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "The patient was admitted for acute on chronic abdominal pain and nausea, consistent with acute on chronic pancreatitis. She had recently left a prior admission AMA but returned due to worsening symptoms and GJ tube dysfunction. Pain and nausea were controlled with IV Dilaudid, Zofran, and Compazine. The GJ tube was successfully replaced by interventional radiology with a preferred type over a wire, and enteral feeds were resumed. Due to poor intake, her Lantus insulin was reduced to 20 units at bedtime, with plans to increase upon improved oral intake. The protonix was switched to Prevacid Solutab for better compatibility with tube administration. The patient declined a final tube function check before discharge. She was discharged home in stable condition with a one-week supply of Dilaudid, instructions to follow up with her PCP for medication refills and insulin adjustments, and advised to monitor GJ tube function.",
    "problems": [
      "Acute pancreatitis",
      "Attention to gastrostomy",
      "Chronic pancreatitis",
      "Diabetes with neurological manifestations, type I [juvenile type], not stated as uncontrolled",
      "Gastroparesis",
      "Iron deficiency anemia, unspecified",
      "Asthma, unspecified type, unspecified"
    ]
  }
}
